        <mxCell id="n16" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n5" target="n6"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n17" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n6" target="n8"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n18" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n6" target="n9"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n19" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n7" target="n8"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n20" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n7" target="n9"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n21" value="writes images today" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeColor=#333333;fontSize=11;exitX=0.96;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n6" target="n10"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n22" value="upload  (opt-in)" style="endArrow=open;endFill=0;dashed=1;html=1;strokeColor=#666666;fontSize=11;exitX=0.5;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="n6" target="n11"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n23" value="Four things this diagram states:&lt;br&gt;1. The API keeps NO state, so it can be replicated. Everything that used to&lt;br&gt;   live in process memory is in Redis now: the catalog cache (single-flight +&lt;br&gt;   fail-open), the ThrottlerModule rate-limit counters, and the websocket&lt;br&gt;   socket lists. That is what makes the x3 above real rather than a target.&lt;br&gt;2. Exactly ONE worker. Cron inside the API would run the reconciliation job&lt;br&gt;   three times, and for a job that moves money that is a serious bug. The&lt;br&gt;   schedule now lives in Redis and each job goes to exactly one worker.&lt;br&gt;   Do NOT raise the worker replica count: cancelExpired reads orders outside&lt;br&gt;   a transaction, so two overlapping sweeps can still refund twice.&lt;br&gt;3. Images are written to the VPS disk by multer. A named Docker volume is&lt;br&gt;   mounted into all three API replicas, so on THIS single VPS they share the&lt;br&gt;   same directory — measured, not assumed. Object storage only becomes&lt;br&gt;   necessary when the replicas move to different machines. An R2 client does&lt;br&gt;   exist in src/catalog/files/storage.service.ts and turns on when the five&lt;br&gt;   R2_* variables are filled; empty means disk.&lt;br&gt;4. Admin is its own deployable on its own hostname, so admin code is never&lt;br&gt;   shipped in the customer bundle. Sessions are per-origin, so an admin who&lt;br&gt;   also sells signs in twice.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Checked against the code on 29/09/2026. The one red box is built but off by&lt;br&gt;default: the R2 client ships in src/, and filling the five R2_* variables&lt;br&gt;switches uploads from the VPS disk to object storage.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The whole cluster has been brought up and measured, not just config-checked:&lt;br&gt;caddy + 3 api + 1 worker + mysql + redis, from an empty volume. 90 requests&lt;br&gt;through caddy were served 31 / 35 / 32 by the three replicas, so the load&lt;br&gt;balancing is real. Rate limiting stayed correct across replicas: one client&lt;br&gt;was cut off at exactly 10 requests while a second client was still served,&lt;br&gt;which is only possible if the counters are shared through Redis and the real&lt;br&gt;client IP survives the proxy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;See DEPLOY.md for the commands and for what is still missing." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fffbe6;strokeColor=#c8a415;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="700" width="740" height="430" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
